os_linux_aarch64: no <fpu_control.h> on android

The aarch64 os layer includes glibc's <fpu_control.h>, which bionic has no
equivalent of:

  os_linux_aarch64.cpp:75:11: fatal error: 'fpu_control.h' file not found

Nothing in the file needs it: init_thread_fpu_state() is empty,
get_fpu_control_word() returns 0 and set_fpu_control_word() does nothing --
aarch64 has no x87 control word to manage. Guard the include and leave the
stubs alone.

Companion to 0006, which does the same for the x86 os layer.

diff --git a/hotspot/src/os_cpu/linux_aarch64/vm/os_linux_aarch64.cpp b/hotspot/src/os_cpu/linux_aarch64/vm/os_linux_aarch64.cpp
index db1cb10..70a8896 100644
--- a/hotspot/src/os_cpu/linux_aarch64/vm/os_linux_aarch64.cpp
+++ b/hotspot/src/os_cpu/linux_aarch64/vm/os_linux_aarch64.cpp
@@ -72,7 +72,9 @@
 # include <pwd.h>
 # include <poll.h>
 # include <ucontext.h>
+#ifndef __ANDROID__
 # include <fpu_control.h>
+#endif
 
 #define REG_FP 29
 
